nsactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-e6bbbb6c6d02465eb276bbf3a403b228","line":24,"path":"rules/migrations.blade.php","start_column":43}],"path":"rules/migrations.blade.php","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"EA2","severity":"MEDIUM","start_column":43,"tags":["Excessive Agency"]},{"category":"Output Handling","code_snippet":"\n## Throttle high-volume exception reports\n\nA failing integration can flood logs or error tracking. Configure `throttle()` with a `Lottery` or `Limit` result to sample or rate-limit matching exception reports. Choose keys deliberately when separate exception classes, tenants, or integrations need independent limits.\n\n## Prevent duplicate reports of one exception instance\n","confidence":0.8,"evidence":{},"finding":"flood log","finding_ids":["finding-8dbfc6b2ae0240f187805a97ddff619c"],"id":"sha256:094a38dbe845c50e16928a4e36aa043dfcfc53094bfb2b3b828674e26ba87f08","intent":null,"line":49,"match_fingerprint":"20b945c1b12b44f7e0991d81616241a739dacb42702f26db27d925baec0e691b","message":"Output size or generation rate is not bounded. Unbounded output enables denial-of-service through resource exhaustion, log flooding, or context-window stuffing.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-8dbfc6b2ae0240f187805a97ddff619c","line":49,"path":"rules/error-handling.md","start_column":26}],"path":"rules/error-handling.md","pattern":"Unbounded Output","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Set explicit limits on output length, generation count, and rate. Use max_tokens and truncation to prevent unbounded output.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"OH3","severity":"MEDIUM","start_column":26,"tags":["Output Handling"]},{"category":"Excessive Agency","code_snippet":"\n## Use `ShouldDispatchAfterCommit` inside transactions\n\nWhen you dispatch an event inside a database transaction, `ShouldDispatchAfterCommit` delays dispatch until all open database transactions commit. If a transaction rolls back, Laravel discards the event. The delay affects synchronous and queued listeners. It is not limited to queue timing.\n\n```php\nclass OrderShipped implements ShouldDispatchAfterCommit {}","confidence":0.7,"evidence":{},"finding":"not limited to","finding_ids":["finding-a393cdafa72545bb8c5e3a7e78804254"],"id":"sha256:b7ca671c71ea8c0a7e64e753ef0819268164f0ecc92ef0c379af43f31eb985f3","intent":null,"line":16,"match_fingerprint":"943d9aae8743c129fe98eb6cc5e984f5e35ceba0b44ce4ca00f42b97f0bf3eaf","message":"Skill's behavior or capabilities extend beyond its stated purpose. Scope creep allows an agent to perform actions unrelated to its documented functionality, increasing the attack surface.","occurrences":[{"finding_id":"finding-a393cdafa72545bb8c5e3a7e78804254","line":16,"path":"rules/events-notifications.blade.php","start_column":262}],"path":"rules/events-notifications.blade.php","pattern":"Scope Creep","raw_count":1,"remediation":"Limit the skill's scope to its documented purpose. Remove instructions that enable the agent to perform actions outside its stated functionality.","review_status":"unreviewed","rule":"EA3","severity":"LOW","start_column":262,"tags":["Excessive Agency"]}],"findings_truncated":false,"freshness":"current","id":"laravel/boost/laravel-best-practices","kind":"standalone_skill","plugin_path":null,"profile":{"digest":"sha256:3a6bac66327c0285edb6012e58fad74604c9d4bd6d3c6dfb0b25d7dcc8f59faf","id":"static-standard-v3"},"raw_finding_count":15,"report_digest":"sha256:d6e284fe69641bd92f31eae24bec1aeeb824a7c27ed9ba566d455f9e00186827","retry":{"attempt_count":1,"disposition":"blocked","latest_status":"partial","next_attempt_at":null,"next_profile":null,"reason":"reference_missing"},"scanned_at":"2026-11-26T12:20:39Z","sca